/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:29:#   - Side gaps only means every emitted beam is diagonal from the start, so the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:33:#     least one marker-controlled sign across same-family gaps, so the rule is
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:39:#   - Old spawn code treated `(dr,dc)` from the gap as the full launch vector.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:40:#     That is replaced with `_launch_dir_from_gap_and_marker`, which combines the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:41:#     side-gap axis with the marker's row/column signs.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:46:#   - Frames still use a 4x4 footprint and keep a gap between bounding boxes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:47:#   - The generator computes launch directions before finalizing gaps and checks
